From 7e9f383ed5de00a1fe8dd0ff5b30a0beb77950a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:37:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(motion): widen a 4-axis wire cut per ruling, uniform
 as a stated choice

Each ruling end takes the widening its own twist and lean need. The
ruled kerf law certifies the emitted wire at every height read. A
transition ruling one millimetre in from each end of a long span ends
a corner's widening; idle transitions are dropped again.

Refs #1170

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
