From b4af149235570462b40d3b7ff9889e613e6ee33c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:38:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(sim): a stated verify tolerance for the wire kerf
 law

The kerf law passes a reading that enters the facets by no more than
the stated tolerance and says the deepest one. A deeper reading is a
gouge that names the tolerance. The threading and slug laws stay strict.

Refs #1170

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
